Duck.ai said

Rollup is treating your entry file—src/main/index.ts—as an external module. That usually means your external option or a plugin’s externalization setting is matching the entry, but Rollup can’t bundle an entry that way. Rollup’s external option is meant for dependencies that should remain outside the bundle. 
rollupjs.org

Check the config used by build:main and look for external, externalize, or a plugin that sets externals. If you use a function or broad pattern, exclude the entry explicitly. For example:

js


external: (id) =>
  id !== 'src/main/index.ts' &&
  /* your existing external checks */
If Rollup passes an absolute path, compare against the resolved entry path instead:

js


import path from 'node:path';

const entry = path.resolve('src/main/index.ts');

export default {
  input: entry,
  external: (id) => id !== entry && /* your existing external checks */,
};
Also check that external isn’t accidentally set to true, or to a pattern that matches all files. If you paste your build:main script and Rollup config, I can point to the exact setting causing it.

