Duck.ai said
The issue is the external check: on Windows, the entry path starts with C:\, not /, so the predicate marks it external.

Import isAbsolute and use it to exclude absolute paths from externalization:

ts


import { isAbsolute, resolve } from "node:path";
import { type UserConfig, defineConfig } from "vite";

// ...

rollupOptions: {
  external: (id: string) =>
    !id.startsWith(".") &&
    !isAbsolute(id) &&
    !id.startsWith("@betterx/"),
},
Save the file, then rerun:

powershell


bun run build:desktop
You said
command to do this

Duck.ai said
From the project root, run this PowerShell command to update the import and external check:

powershell


(Get-Content packages/desktop/vite.main.config.ts -Raw) `
  -replace 'import \{ resolve \} from "node:path";', 'import { isAbsolute, resolve } from "node:path";' `
  -replace '!id\.startsWith\("\."\) && !id\.startsWith\("\/"\)', '!id.startsWith(".") && !isAbsolute(id)' |
  Set-Content packages/desktop/vite.main.config.ts
Then rebuild:

powershell


bun run build:desktop
