You said
Installer failed with exit code: 1603

Duck.ai said

Exit code 1603 is a generic Windows Installer failure, so it doesn’t identify the cause by itself. Try opening PowerShell as Administrator, then run:

powershell


winget install --id OpenJS.NodeJS.22 --exact
If it fails again, copy the installer log path shown in the output and run:

powershell


Select-String -Path "PASTE_LOG_PATH_HERE" -Pattern "Return value 3" -Context 8,5
Paste that result here; it should reveal the specific install failure. 
Microsoft

