Avoid the MSI downgrade conflict by using Node 22 as a temporary portable copy. From the project root, run:

powershell


Invoke-WebRequest https://nodejs.org/dist/v22.23.5/node-v22.23.5-win-x64.zip -OutFile "$env:TEMP\node22.zip"
Expand-Archive "$env:TEMP\node22.zip" "$env:TEMP\node22" -Force

$env:force_no_cache = 'true'
& "$env:TEMP\node22\node.exe" .\node_modules\.bun\electron@42.3.0\node_modules\electron\install.js
Remove-Item Env:force_no_cache

Test-Path .\node_modules\.bun\electron@42.3.0\node_modules\electron\path.txt
Node 22.23.5 is an official LTS release. If the final check says True, start the app with:

powershell


bun run start:desktop
