TXT
Duck.ai said

Nothing you pasted deleted Node or your project files. Remove-Item Env:force_no_cache only cleared a temporary setting, and undo isn’t a PowerShell command.

The console still shows Node v26.12.1, and the downloaded ZIP didn’t extract, so Node 22 isn’t available at the path you tried. I also gave you the wrong executable path earlier—sorry. Try downloading the archive with curl.exe, then locate node.exe inside it:

powershell


Remove-Item "$env:TEMP\node22.zip" -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
curl.exe -L "https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v22.x/node-v22.23.5-win-x64.zip" -o "$env:TEMP\node22.zip"
Get-Item "$env:TEMP\node22.zip" | Select-Object Length
The file should be about 36 MB. If it is, extract it and run the Electron installer using the Node 22 executable:

powershell


Expand-Archive "$env:TEMP\node22.zip" "$env:TEMP\node22" -Force
$node22 = Get-ChildItem "$env:TEMP\node22" -Filter node.exe -Recurse | Select-Object -First 1
& $node22.FullName --version
& $node22.FullName .\node_modules\.bun\electron@42.3.0\node_modules\electron\install.js
Node 22.23.5 is listed in the official Node.js 22 release archive. 
